ns rather than relying on external equation numbers. The proof defect is an inference gap, not an absent target statement.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The main declared local constructions (D, F, covers, projections, intervals, and measures) have stated introductions. The prose also uses many mathematical objects and quantified variables through inline descriptions; an inventory alone cannot establish every such occurrence. In particular, the named singleton in S001 does not discharge the separate proof obligation that its dimension is zero.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Actual factual uses in S001 include the unproved singleton Hausdorff-dimension assertion. It is neither a listed input nor an earlier local result. Thus the inference's factual dependency closure fails at that point, even though the later named theorem uses are listed.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/0/uses\",\"/inference/argument/0/produces\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Mathematical conditional judgment from this packet alone: it does not suffice, because S001's n=0 inference to D=0 is unsupported locally or by a listed input. I read the full packet and the relevant declared Yui rules; I make no claim of runtime isolation or carrier attestation. Those execution checks do not alter this mathematical failure.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/logic/primitives/1\",\"/output/statement\"]}}}}"}

